{"name":"Jet d’Eau","hex":"#d1eaec","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Manem."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A collimated stream, spurt or flow of liquid or gas from a pressurized container, an engine, etc.","A spout or nozzle for creating a jet of fluid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jet d'Eau","blocks":[{"text":"The Jet d'Eau is a large fountain in Geneva, Switzerland, and is one of the city's most famous landmarks, being featured on the city's official tourism web site. Situated where Lake Geneva exits as the Rhône, it is visible throughout the city and from the air, even when flying over Geneva at an altitude of ten kilometres (33,000 ft)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Jet_d%27eau_de_Gen%C3%A8ve_%28swiss%29.jpg/330px-Jet_d%27eau_de_Gen%C3%A8ve_%28swiss%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jet_d'Eau","wikidata":"Q684661"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Jet_d%27eau_1886.jpg/500px-Jet_d%27eau_1886.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Jet_d%27eau_1886.jpg/1280px-Jet_d%27eau_1886.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Jet_d%27eau_1886.jpg/500px-Jet_d%27eau_1886.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The first jet d'eau, around 1886.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJet_d'eau_1886.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/View_of_Jet_D%27eau_from_St_Pierre_Cathedral.jpg/500px-View_of_Jet_D%27eau_from_St_Pierre_Cathedral.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u